s a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.cor-257-logarithmic-separation"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.cor-257-logarithmic-separation"],"id":"long.cor-257-logarithmic-separation","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Corollary 13.2 (finite-functional separation)","locator":"Long record Corollary 13.2, p. 144, label cor:257-logarithmic-separation","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For every finite nonempty $F$, with $Q=\\operatorname{lcm}(F)$,\n$$\n\n K_*(F)\\ge\\max_{\\ell\\mid Q}\n   \\mathbb P\\bigl(U_F(N)>1\\mid\\ell\\mid N\\bigr),\n$$\nwhere $N$ is uniform modulo $Q$. The supports of Theorem 13.1 satisfy $K_*(F)\\ge1-e^{-1}$ and $\\kappa_1(F;1)\\le30\\log2/H$. In particular, no absolute $C$ gives $K_*(F)\\le C\\kappa_1(F;1)$ for all finite nonempty $F$, even after all covering sets, exponents, coefficients and positive weights have been optimised.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.cor-257-logarithmic-separation","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.cor-257-logarithmic-separation","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.cor-257-logarithmic-separation%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.exists_support_paperCoverCost_ge%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.cor-257-logarithmic-separation%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.exists_support_paperCoverCost_ge%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.exists_support_paperCoverCost_ge"